{"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sink","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","title":"sink()","externalID":"s:10GLibObject15ClosureProtocolPAAE4sinkyyF","modules":[{"name":"GLibObject"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GLibObject","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureProtocol\/sink()"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes over the initial ownership of a closure."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sink"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each closure is initially created in a “floating” state, which means"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"that the initial reference count is not owned by any caller."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This function checks to see if the object is still floating, and if so,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unsets the floating state and decreases the reference count. If the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure is not floating, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_closure_sink()"},{"type":"text","text":" does nothing."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The reason for the existence of the floating state is to prevent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"cumbersome code sequences like:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"(C Language Example):","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["closure = g_cclosure_new (cb_func, cb_data);","g_source_set_closure (source, closure);","g_closure_unref (closure); \/\/ GObject doesn't really need this"],"syntax":"C"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because "},{"code":"g_source_set_closure()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (and similar functions) take ownership of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"initial reference count, if it is unowned, we instead can write:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"(C Language Example):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"C","type":"codeListing","code":["g_source_set_closure (source, g_cclosure_new (cb_func, cb_data));"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Generally, this function is used together with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_closure_ref()"},{"type":"text","text":". An example"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of storing a closure for later notification looks like:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(C Language Example):"}]},{"code":["static GClosure *notify_closure = NULL;","void","foo_notify_set_closure (GClosure *closure)","{","  if (notify_closure)","    g_closure_unref (notify_closure);","  notify_closure = closure;","  if (notify_closure)","    {","      g_closure_ref (notify_closure);","      g_closure_sink (notify_closure);","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"C"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_closure_sink()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" may decrement the reference count of a closure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(if it hasn’t been called on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"closure"},{"text":" yet) just like ","type":"text"},{"code":"g_closure_unref()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"g_closure_ref()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" should be called prior to this function.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glibobject\/closureprotocol\/sink()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject","doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureProtocol"]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject/ClosureProtocol":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClosureProtocol"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureProtocol","url":"\/documentation\/glibobject\/closureprotocol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"GClosure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" represents a callback supplied by the programmer."}],"title":"ClosureProtocol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ClosureProtocol","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject/ClosureProtocol/sink()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes over the initial ownership of a closure."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/ClosureProtocol\/sink()","title":"sink()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glibobject\/closureprotocol\/sink()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sink","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}]},"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glibobject","title":"GLibObject","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"}}}